{"module":"Term 1","title":"Unit 2 — Education","description":"School life, the past simple and past continuous, expressing likes and dislikes.","intro":"This unit deals with school, subjects, learning and memories of school life.","objectifs":["Talk about school subjects and systems.","Use the past simple and the past continuous.","Express likes and dislikes."],"cours":[{"t":"Vocabulary: school and learning","h":"<ul><li>primary / middle / secondary school, university, Common Core</li><li>subjects: maths, physics, biology, history, philosophy</li><li>to pass / fail an exam, to revise, a timetable, a degree, a scholarship, to drop out</li></ul>"},{"t":"Grammar: past simple and past continuous","h":"<ul><li><b>Past simple</b> — finished actions: <i>I <b>passed</b> my exam last year.</i> Irregular verbs: go → went, write → wrote, take → took.</li><li><b>Past continuous</b> (was / were + verb-ing) — an action in progress in the past: <i>I <b>was revising</b> at 9 p.m.</i></li><li>Together: <i>I <b>was reading</b> when the teacher <b>came</b> in.</i> (long action interrupted by a short one)</li></ul><div class=\"formula key\">while + past continuous / when + past simple</div>"},{"t":"Communication: likes and dislikes","h":"<ul><li>I love / really like / enjoy + verb-ing</li><li>I don’t mind…</li><li>I can’t stand / hate + verb-ing</li></ul>"}],"recap":"Past simple = finished action (went, studied). Past continuous = action in progress (was studying). “I was studying when the phone rang.” Likes: enjoy / love + -ing; dislikes: hate / can’t stand + -ing.","cards":[["Past continuous","was / were + verb-ing"],["when / while","when + past simple ; while + past continuous"],["to drop out","To leave school before finishing."],["enjoy","Followed by verb-ing: I enjoy reading."]],"exercises":{"facile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Yesterday I ___ my homework.","choices":["did","do","was do","done"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Yesterday” → past simple of “do” = did."},{"type":"direct","q":"Past simple of “go”:","accept":["went"],"display":"went","explain":"Irregular verb: go – went – gone."},{"type":"qcm","q":"To leave school before finishing your studies is to…","choices":["drop out","graduate","revise","pass"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Drop out” = abandon school."}],"moyen":[{"type":"qcm","q":"I ___ when the teacher came in.","choices":["was writing","wrote","am writing","write"],"answer":0,"explain":"A long action in progress (past continuous) interrupted by a short one (past simple)."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete: I really enjoy ___ (read) novels.","accept":["reading"],"display":"reading","explain":"“Enjoy” is followed by verb-ing."},{"type":"qcm","q":"Choose the correct sentence:","choices":["While she was studying, her brother was watching TV.","While she studied, her brother watch TV.","When she was study, her brother watched TV.","While she is studying, her brother was watching TV."],"answer":0,"explain":"Two actions in progress at the same time in the past → past continuous for both."}],"difficile":[{"type":"qcm","q":"Which sentence is correct?","choices":["When I arrived, the lesson had already started.","When I was arriving, the lesson started already.","When I arrive, the lesson was starting already.","When I arrived, the lesson already start."],"answer":0,"explain":"Past simple for the arrival; an action finished before it (past perfect) is the natural choice."},{"type":"direct","q":"Complete with the right form: “They ___ (not / study) when I called them.” (contracted form)","accept":["weren't studying","were not studying"],"display":"weren't studying","explain":"Negative past continuous: were not (weren’t) + -ing."},{"type":"qcm","q":"“I can’t stand ___ up early.”","choices":["getting","to getting","get","got"],"answer":0,"explain":"“Can’t stand” is followed by verb-ing."}]}}